From 0d53a59c8791af68a6a531fe9f77c13a5bd17204 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:51:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Write deterministic keys for pickled and IOSpec values in
 exports

The exporter keyed pickle_data and io_data by id() of each value, so the
generated modules, _mx_io.py and _mx_pickled differed between two exports
of the same model. Keys are now running numbers: IOSpecs in the order of
Model.iospecs, pickled values in the order the translators first ask for
them. ModuleClassPickler refers to a user module by the same number.

The loader treats the keys as opaque, so what an exported model loads is
unchanged. The new test exports one saved model in two processes with
different hash seeds and compares every file.
