diff --git a/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst b/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst
index cf831b0..3a4684a 100644
--- a/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst
+++ b/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst
@@ -150,6 +150,18 @@ Backward Incompatible Changes
 Bug Fixes
 ============
 
+* An exported model no longer depends on memory addresses. The exporter
+  wrote the :func:`id` of each pickled value and of each IOSpec value as
+  its key in the package, so two exports of one model differed. The keys
+  are now running numbers in the order of the model. Exporting the same
+  model twice with the same Python version on the same platform writes
+  the same Python modules, and the same pickle file unless a pickled
+  value is a :class:`set` or :class:`frozenset` of str or bytes, whose
+  pickle follows hash order, which changes between processes with
+  ``PYTHONHASHSEED``. The pickle protocol and the newlines of the Python
+  modules follow the Python version and the platform. Excel files that
+  openpyxl writes still record the time they were written.
+
 * :meth:`Cells.values<modelx.core.cells.Cells.values>` and
   :meth:`Cells.items<modelx.core.cells.Cells.items>` now return the stored
   values of a Cells with one parameter whose argument is a tuple, and of a
